      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Phantom 1.3B detailer (Q8) (t2v)\n\nhttps://huggingface.co/QuantStack/Phantom_Wan_1.3B-GGUF\n\nnot using speed up loras initially, so might need more cfg and higher steps.\n\nmaybe test at denoise 1.0 to see what it does at each then dial back if its worth it. \n\n---\n\n# TESTS:\n\ninbound is only upscaled x2 (orig: 480 x 192) so could push to 720p which is max for phantom 1.3b model (1721 x 710 in 2.39:1 ratio, so upscale by 3 not 2 would be better but will add time). \n\n\n- 8 steps. cfg 1. denoise 0.6. result was foggy. took 500 seconds. this needs a speed up lora.\n\n# ADDED IN THIS LORA, CONTINUED TESTS:\n\n`Wan21_CausVid_bidirect2_T2V_1_3B_lora_rank32.safetensors` from Kijai https://huggingface.co/Kijai/WanVideo_comfy/blob/main/Wan21_CausVid_bidirect2_T2V_1_3B_lora_rank32.safetensors\n\nbased on some notes here - https://www.reddit.com/r/StableDiffusion/comments/1knuafk/causvid_lora_massive_speedup_for_wan21_made_by/\n\n- 4 steps, cfg 1, denoise 0.6. finished in 251 seconds (4 mins). result stronger but its changed everything in background to blocks though it might not matter once run through LTX. also got a weird effect in first frames. but face is good. testing lower denoise.\n\n- 4 steps. cfg 1. denoise 0.25. hot damn finished in 250 seconds (4 mins) and is probably the best results I have seen yet. I am now wondering if it might not be best used in the detailing setup at very end for 1920 finalising. Its still fake face but for a fix on a 480 its  as good as I would need. only issue is the weird first frame explosion not sure how that will impact LTX but I always cut off bookends in post anyway because of that kind of shiz.\n\n*(also can try lower strength on lora but more steps. also try ultrawan lora for 4K and 1K its made for 1.3B, also try without VAE decode tiled or change its settings, its a time consumer.)*.\n\n- tested the above with Ultrawan 4K lora added in. (I set to 1 strenght but found notes saying use 0.25 to 0.5 and that the 4K causes black screen). RESULT: str 1 caused dream movement effects, too strong. reducing to str 0.25 to test again (0.25 denoise). RESULT: works but I feel like it is better without it. testing Ultrawan 1K, same 0.25 str settings, just to confirm. (note: errors in lora window so probably not working fully with 1K) RESULT: possibly slightly better. something to trial longer.\n\nend result was good. I now need to test this with higher detailer 1920p for final polish.\n\n## HIGH END DETAILER POLISHER (i.e. at 1920x 768 inbound video 241 frames at 24fps)\n\n- change inbound to 1920 full size end result video.\n- disable upscaling\n- reduce denoise from 0.25 to 0.2\n- run it.\n\n- its blapping the GPU at this size. VAE encoding took ages to switched from fp32 to bf16 encoder. still taking ages so I dont think this model will deal with 1920 x 768 at all for 241 frames at 24fps. Try it in the USDU loader maybe. 10 mins in was still waiting to see a notch on the main sampler. gave up."
